# compdump
#
# zsh writes the completion system's tables to a dump file that the next
# compinit reads back instead of scanning $fpath.  This shell writes none:
# the file would be read by the other shell too, and the two must not trade
# one another's files.  So this is the name a startup file may call, and it
# does nothing, at 0.  See compinit, and docs/spec/functions.md.

return 0
